    "title": "Where to watch Guardians vs Mariners game on Sunday, March 29",
    "text": "Updated March 29, 2026, 1:12 p.m. ETThe fourth game of a four-game series between the Cleveland Guardians and Seattle Mariners to open the 2026 MLB season will be played Sunday, March 29.The Guardians got out to a good start with a season-opening road win against Seattle on the strength of rookie outfielder Chase DeLauter's two-homer effort combined with a solid start from Opening Day starter Tanner Bibee.They'll look to close out the opening series with another win, but fans will need a certain streaming service in order to watch.Here's how Guardians fans can tune in. Are the Guardians on TV today vs. Mariners and when do they play on Sunday, March 29?The final game of the four-game set between the Guardians and Mariners has a scheduled first pitch of 7:20 p.m. ET Sunday.The game will streaming exclusively on Peacock, NBC's streaming app.Who are the projected starters for Sunday's Guardians vs Mariners game?For the Guardians, Slade Cecconi will toe the rubber as the starting pitcher. The 26-year-old righty started 23 games for Cleveland a season ago, finishing the season with a 7-7 record and a 4.30 ERA. He struck out 109 batters over 132 innings, allowing just 32 bases on balls.For Seattle, the starter will be 26-year-old Emerson Hancock. Hancock pitched in 22 games a season ago (16 starts), compiling a 4-5 record to go with a 4.90 ERA. He gave up 15 home runs in 90 innings throughout 2025.The Akron Beacon Journal sports department can be contacted via email at bjsports@thebeaconjournal.com.",
